---
import Lab from '../layouts/Lab.astro';
import { releases } from '../data/site';
import { fmtBytes, fmtDate, v } from '../lib/format';

const latest = releases.autobot.latest;
const apk = latest.assets.find((a) => /release\.apk$/.test(a.name));
const sums = latest.assets.find((a) => a.name === 'SHA256SUMS.txt');
const hash = releases.autobot.checksums?.split('\n').find((l) => l.includes('release.apk'))?.split(/\s+/)[0];
const cert = '9a1378acf9587885e7920355558c85a1ec0e89304f58c153feebf90fdee7f3f1';
---
<Lab
  path="/install/"
  current="install"
  title="Install"
  description="Install Autobot on Android or iOS, or install the Autobot Agent on a desktop or VPS. Requirements, verification and first run."
>
  <p class="label">Autobot · install</p>
  <h1>Install</h1>
  <p class="lede">Android 14 or newer on arm64, iOS 18 or newer, or a desktop machine for the agent. No account is required for any of them.</p>
  <p class="meta">Latest v{v(latest.tag)} · {fmtDate(latest.published)} · <a href="/verify/">verify first</a></p>

  <dl class="facts">
    <div><dt>Android</dt><dd>14+ · arm64</dd></div>
    <div><dt>iOS</dt><dd>18+ · TestFlight</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Agent</dt><dd>macOS arm64 · Linux</dd></div>
    <div><dt>APK</dt><dd>{apk ? fmtBytes(apk.size) : 'signed'}</dd></div>
    <div><dt>License</dt><dd>Apache-2.0</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Account</dt><dd>None</dd></div>
  </dl>

  <section>
    <h2>Android</h2>
    <h3>1. Download the signed APK</h3>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button button--primary" href={apk?.url} download>Download {v(latest.tag)}</a>
      {sums && <a class="text-link" href={sums.url} rel="noopener">SHA256SUMS.txt ↗</a>}
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:14px">The file is <code>{apk?.name}</code>. Android will ask you to allow installs from your browser or file manager.</p>

    <h3>2. Check the hash and the signer</h3>
    <pre><code><span class="comment"># compare the full line with SHA256SUMS.txt</span>
shasum -a 256 {apk?.name}
<span class="comment"># {hash ?? 'see SHA256SUMS.txt'}</span>

<span class="comment"># print the signing certificate</span>
apksigner verify --print-certs {apk?.name}
<span class="comment"># signer SHA-256: {cert}</span></code></pre>
    <p class="small">The certificate is pinned in the repository. If the hash or the signer does not match, stop.</p>

    <h3>3. First run</h3>
    <ol>
      <li>Open <strong>MODELS</strong>. The app measures RAM, free storage and CPU features, then labels each model FITS, TIGHT or TOO BIG.</li>
      <li>Download a model. Transfers resume with HTTP Range and are checked against the hub’s SHA-256. A mismatch deletes the file.</li>
      <li>Switch the network to <strong>Offline</strong> if you want. Chat, agents, images, voice and recipes continue on the phone.</li>
      <li>Optional: add a cloud provider. Turn on redaction and “phone first” if you want the local model to answer first.</li>
    </ol>
    <div class="note"><strong>No model is bundled.</strong> The app starts with no model and says so. Model weights are large; choosing the right one for the device is better than shipping a compromise.</div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>iOS</h2>
    <p>TestFlight, app id <code>ai.wckd.autobot</code>. The app runs the same Kotlin Multiplatform core as Android: agent runtime, network policy, redaction, settings, model management and the <code>.autobot</code> export format.</p>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Value</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Bundle ID</td><td class="mono">ai.wckd.autobot</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Minimum</td><td>iOS 18</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Engines</td><td>Metal, Core ML, whisper.cpp</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Build</td><td><a href="https://github.com/wckdboy/autobot/blob/main/ios/README.md" rel="noopener">ios/README.md ↗</a></td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Autobot Agent</h2>
    <p>The same agent as the phone’s, for a desktop or VPS. One script installs the agent and Invincible Gateway, verifies the release, installs llama.cpp if it is missing, and runs <code>autobot setup</code>. No root.</p>
    <pre><code>curl -fsSL https://invincible.sh/install.sh | sh</code></pre>
    <h3>What setup asks</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Network:</strong> offline, direct, Tor or SOCKS5 for the whole machine.</li>
      <li><strong>Model:</strong> a Qwen open-weights model sized to the machine’s memory, or any <code>hf:</code> GGUF.</li>
      <li><strong>Agent:</strong> its working directory, and whether turns stay on local models (the default).</li>
      <li><strong>Telegram:</strong> optional. A bot token from @BotFather; approvals arrive as buttons.</li>
      <li><strong>Background:</strong> launchd on macOS; systemd user units with linger on Linux.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Then:</p>
    <pre><code>autobot            <span class="comment"># chat in the terminal</span>
autobot code       <span class="comment"># work in this directory</span>
autobot doctor     <span class="comment"># check the gateway, model, tools and services</span></code></pre>
    <p class="small">macOS arm64, Linux x86_64 and arm64. Signed release, pinned key, reproducible Linux builds. <a href="https://invincible.sh/install/" rel="noopener">Full gateway install notes ↗</a></p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
    <details>
      <summary>The APK will not install</summary>
      <div class="details-body"><p>Autobot needs Android 14 or newer and an arm64 device. Check Settings → About phone. If an older Autobot build is installed with a different key, uninstall it first; the release key is <code>autobot-release-2026</code>.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>The app opens but there is no model</summary>
      <div class="details-body"><p>That is the default. Open MODELS, pick a model marked FITS or TIGHT, and download it. Keep the screen on until the download completes if your device aggressively stops background work.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>A download fails the hash check</summary>
      <div class="details-body"><p>The file is deleted and not used. Retry once. A repeated failure usually means a proxy, captive portal or truncated transfer; switch networks and try again.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Where is the network switch?</summary>
      <div class="details-body"><p>Privacy Center. The global mode starts at Offline. Direct, Tor and SOCKS5 are opt-in; each provider can override the route, but cannot downgrade a global Tor or SOCKS5 mode to Direct.</p></div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>How do I check the agent’s install script?</summary>
      <div class="details-body"><p>The site serves a verbatim mirror with a recorded SHA-256. The upstream script checks a signed <code>SHA256SUMS</code> against a pinned key before installing. Manual commands are on <a href="/verify/">Verify</a>.</p></div>
    </details>
  </section>
</Lab>
